  "caption": "By week three of a trail challenge, the outside of Quinn's ankle was grumbling on bumpy ground.\n\nOuter-ankle ache like this often involves the peroneal tendons. After old sprains, balance sense can dull, so these stabilisers work overtime, and a sudden jump in load can tip them over the edge. Resting or bracing forever usually isn't the answer.\n\nWhat often helps: easing terrain for a while, band work pushing the foot outwards, slow even calf raises, balance retraining (one leg, then wobbly ground, then eyes closed), and bringing uneven trails back last.\n\nA tendon flicking over the ankle bone, sudden sharp pain after an injury, big swelling, or no change after about six weeks of rehab is worth getting checked.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
